# Tasks: BUG-REGISTRY

Purpose:
  First-class BUG artifact system for the delivery workflow. A BUG is a
  persistent, tracked defect record — distinct from runtime failure
  classification (FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd maps an error to a type;
  this registry tracks the defect across steps, occurrences, and fixes).
  Blocking BUGs stop the flow: no continuation to the next workflow step
  while the current step has an open blocking BUG.

Owns:
  BUG artifact format
  Duplicate-detection protocol
  Block semantics
  Resolution protocol

Storage:
  .sdd/projects/{project}/bugs/BUG-XXX.sdd (one artifact per BUG)
  Index: .sdd/projects/{project}/bugs/INDEX.sdd (status board)

ArtifactFormat (all fields mandatory):
  ID:            BUG-<seq>                     (BUG-001, BUG-002, ...)
  DetectedAt:    <ISO-8601>
  WorkflowStep:  <short key>                    (e.g. BE, CR-API, DC-TS)
  Description:   <what is wrong>
  Expected:      <what should be>
  Actual:        <what happens>
  AffectedFiles: [<paths>]
  RelatedSteps:  [<short keys impacted or implicated>]
  Occurrences:   <append-only list; each entry: timestamp, step, context>
  Status:        OPEN -> RESOLVED
  (on resolution) ResolvedAt, FixVerified: YES|NO, AffectedStepReRun: PASS|FAIL

DuplicateDetectionProtocol:
  Before creating a BUG:
    1. Search existing unresolved (Status: OPEN) BUG cases.
    2. Check whether the same or a related issue already exists
       (same root cause OR same affected artifact).
    3. If it EXISTS:
       - Do NOT create a duplicate.
       - Append a new Occurrence to the existing BUG: timestamp, current
         workflow step, affected files.
    4. If it does NOT exist: create a new BUG artifact + index entry.
  Rule: one root cause = one BUG; occurrences accumulate, never fork.

CreationTriggers (from any step):
  broken requirements, contradictions, missing dependencies,
  implementation failures, inconsistent artifacts, unexpected behavior,
  failed validation.

BlockSemantics:
  On BUG creation at step S:
    1. STOP — do not continue past S.
    2. Mark S as BLOCKED (TASK-STATE-MACHINE: ANY_STATE -> BLOCKED).
    3. Record blocking_bugs[] in the delivery run state (chains/delivery.sdd
       StepState) or task state.
  While a blocking BUG is open at S:
    - The next /next MUST return to S's blocked state, NOT advance.
    - VR is unreachable ([DL1-6]).
  BUGs in non-blocking branches (parallel branch B has a BUG, other
  branches proceed) — the FLOW continues in other branches, but AN/VR
  still wait for the blocked branch to resolve.

ResolutionProtocol:
  After a BUG fix is applied:
    1. VERIFY FIX     — the fix itself is validated (tests, evidence).
    2. RE-RUN AFFECTED STEP — the step where the BUG was detected re-executes.
    3. VALIDATE RESULT — step output re-checked against its DONE criteria.
    4. MARK BUG RESOLVED — Status: RESOLVED, FixVerified: YES, timestamp.
    5. CONTINUE WORKFLOW — state returns to pre-block; /next proceeds.
  Rule: resolving one BUG does NOT mark unrelated steps as completed —
        only the affected step's re-run counts ([DL1-4] still applies).

CrossLinks:
  FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd — runtime error classification; a classified
    failure becomes a BUG record when it blocks a step (classification is
    the trigger's evidence).
  chains/bugfix.sdd (B1) — the FIX execution chain for the code side.
  LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd — guards fix->retest loops; BUG Occurrences feed
    DuplicateActionDetection (same bug re-detected = repeat, blocked).
  chains/delivery.sdd — StepState.blocking_bugs + [DL1-5].

Rules:
  [BG1] Every blocking defect MUST become a BUG record — never a chat note.
  [BG2] Search-before-create is MANDATORY; duplicates are forbidden.
  [BG3] Occurrences are append-only; existing BUGs are never forked.
  [BG4] A blocking BUG stops its step and the flow at that step.
  [BG5] Resolution requires fix verification + affected-step re-run.
  [BG6] BUG resolution never completes unrelated steps.
  [BG7] BUG artifacts are project-scoped and git-versioned (audit trail).

Navigation:
  FailureClassification: @FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd
  TaskStateMachine: @TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  LoopProtection: @LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
  BugfixChain: @../chains/bugfix.sdd
  DeliveryChain: @../chains/delivery.sdd
  DoneProof: @DONE-PROOF.sdd
  TasksIndex: @INDEX.sdd

State: +
